{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656102",
      "title": "Understanding the Component Lifecycle",
      "lectureOrder": 401,
      "videoOrder": 370,
      "sourceHash": "aff23bf64647f9f3801aa2188e622f892d26b1f11b3bbd4fd0a385db5011b8d7",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.73,
          "end": 3.69,
          "en": "-: Woo!",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.69,
          "end": 5.4,
          "en": "We're nearing the end of the section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.4,
          "end": 8.19,
          "en": "but there's one thing you might have recognized before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.19,
          "end": 10.26,
          "en": "where you weren't sure what it does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.26,
          "end": 12.21,
          "en": "What's up with this ngOnInit method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.21,
          "end": 15.42,
          "en": "we have in new components created through the CLI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.42,
          "end": 16.593,
          "en": "What's it doing?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.43,
          "end": 19.68,
          "en": "NgOnInit is a lifecycle hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.68,
          "end": 22.68,
          "en": "and Angular supports a couple of lifecycle hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.68,
          "end": 24.48,
          "en": "Let's take a closer look.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 24.48,
          "end": 27.48,
          "en": "If a new component is created in Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.48,
          "end": 29.76,
          "en": "and of course Angular is responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.76,
          "end": 31.08,
          "en": "for creating these components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 31.08,
          "end": 33.39,
          "en": "when it finds one of our selectors for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 33.39,
          "end": 35.7,
          "en": "it will instantiate a new version of that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 35.7,
          "end": 37.89,
          "en": "and add it into the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 37.89,
          "end": 40.32,
          "en": "So once a new component is instantiated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 40.32,
          "end": 43.71,
          "en": "Angular goes through a couple of different phases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 43.71,
          "end": 46.05,
          "en": "in this creation process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 46.05,
          "end": 47.82,
          "en": "And it will actually give us a chance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 47.82,
          "end": 52.08,
          "en": "to hook into these phases and execute some code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 52.08,
          "end": 55.47,
          "en": "We can hook into these phases by implementing some methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 55.47,
          "end": 58.89,
          "en": "Angular will call, if they are present.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 58.89,
          "end": 60.39,
          "en": "The first phase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 60.39,
          "end": 64.11,
          "en": "the first hook we can hook into is ngOnChanges.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 64.11,
          "end": 67.08,
          "en": "And this may actually be executed multiple times.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 67.08,
          "end": 68.7,
          "en": "It's executed right at the start,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 68.7,
          "end": 70.56,
          "en": "when a new component is created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 70.56,
          "end": 71.52,
          "en": "But thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 71.52,
          "end": 73.38,
          "en": "it's also always called,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 73.38,
          "end": 77.22,
          "en": "whenever one of our bound input properties changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 77.22,
          "end": 81.24,
          "en": "And with that, I mean, properties decorated with \"@input\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 81.24,
          "end": 84.423,
          "en": "so whenever these properties receive new values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 85.38,
          "end": 88.44,
          "en": "Now the second hook is ngOnInit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 88.44,
          "end": 90.15,
          "en": "This method gets executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 90.15,
          "end": 92.61,
          "en": "once the component has been initialized.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 92.61,
          "end": 94.59,
          "en": "This does not mean that we can see it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 94.59,
          "end": 97.11,
          "en": "It has not been added to the DOM, yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 97.11,
          "end": 99.63,
          "en": "so to say, it has not been displayed yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 99.63,
          "end": 102.69,
          "en": "but Angular finished the basic initialization.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 102.69,
          "end": 104.61,
          "en": "Our properties can now be accessed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 104.61,
          "end": 106.47,
          "en": "and initialized, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 106.47,
          "end": 109.92,
          "en": "So the object was created, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 109.92,
          "end": 111,
          "en": "And if you are interested,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 111,
          "end": 114.36,
          "en": "ngOnInit will run after the constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 114.36,
          "end": 116.03999999999999,
          "en": "Then, we have ngDoCheck.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 116.03999999999999,
          "end": 118.62,
          "en": "That will also run multiple times.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 118.62,
          "end": 121.98,
          "en": "Actually, this method will be executed a lot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 121.98,
          "end": 125.37,
          "en": "because this will run whenever change detection runs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 125.37,
          "end": 127.44,
          "en": "Now change detection simply is the system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 127.44,
          "end": 129.18,
          "en": "by which Angular determines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 129.18,
          "end": 132.36,
          "en": "whether something changed on the template of a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 132.36,
          "end": 134.31,
          "en": "or inside of a component I should say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 134.31,
          "end": 137.52,
          "en": "So whether it needs to change something in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 137.52,
          "end": 139.71,
          "en": "So whether some property value change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 139.71,
          "end": 142.02,
          "en": "from one to two, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 142.02,
          "end": 144.75,
          "en": "and that property's output in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 144.75,
          "end": 146.88,
          "en": "Well, of course Angular needs to re-render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 146.88,
          "end": 148.44,
          "en": "that part of the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 148.44,
          "end": 151.5,
          "en": "And ngDoCheck is a hook executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 151.5,
          "end": 153.99,
          "en": "on every check Angular makes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 153.99,
          "end": 156.6,
          "en": "Now important on every check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 156.6,
          "end": 158.85,
          "en": "So not just if something changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 158.85,
          "end": 161.573,
          "en": "A lot of times ngDoCheck will run",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 161.573,
          "end": 163.26,
          "en": "because you clicked some button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 163.26,
          "end": 167.07,
          "en": "which doesn't change anything, but still it's an event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 167.07,
          "end": 170.28,
          "en": "and on events, Angular has to check if something changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 170.28,
          "end": 171.78,
          "en": "because how else would it know?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 171.78,
          "end": 172.8,
          "en": "You don't tell it, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 172.8,
          "end": 175.53,
          "en": "So it has to check on certain triggering events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 175.53,
          "end": 178.59,
          "en": "like you clicked somewhere, or a timer fired,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 178.59,
          "end": 180.87,
          "en": "or an observable was resolved.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 180.87,
          "end": 184.02,
          "en": "And on these occasions, it will check your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 184.02,
          "end": 186.6,
          "en": "and ngDoCheck will be executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 186.6,
          "end": 189.06,
          "en": "Now, whilst this might sound very inefficient,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 189.06,
          "end": 191.16,
          "en": "Angular does this in a very efficient way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 191.16,
          "end": 193.62,
          "en": "So change detection, Angular works pretty great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 193.62,
          "end": 195.84,
          "en": "and doesn't cost a lot of performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 195.84,
          "end": 198.3,
          "en": "NgDoCheck is a great method to use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 198.3,
          "end": 201.81,
          "en": "if you want to do something on every change detection cycle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 201.81,
          "end": 205.71,
          "en": "like maybe, manually inform Angular about some change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 205.71,
          "end": 208.23,
          "en": "it would not be able to detect otherwise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 208.23,
          "end": 210.513,
          "en": "though that is a very advanced use case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 211.35,
          "end": 214.38,
          "en": "Well then, we reach AfterContentInit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 214.38,
          "end": 216.63,
          "en": "This is called whenever the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 216.63,
          "end": 220.82999999999998,
          "en": "which is projected via ng-content has been initialized.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 220.82999999999998,
          "end": 223.41,
          "en": "So not the view of the component itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 223.41,
          "end": 226.8,
          "en": "but instead you could say, the view of the parent component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 226.8,
          "end": 230.49,
          "en": "especially a part which will get added to our component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 230.49,
          "end": 232.23,
          "en": "through ng-content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 232.23,
          "end": 234.9,
          "en": "An ngAfterContentInit check is executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 234.9,
          "end": 237,
          "en": "whenever change detection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 237,
          "end": 242,
          "en": "checked this content we're projecting into our component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 242.37,
          "end": 244.68,
          "en": "NgAfterViewInit is then reached,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 244.68,
          "end": 248.22,
          "en": "once the view of our own component has been",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 248.22,
          "end": 249.48,
          "en": "finished initializing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 249.48,
          "end": 252.81,
          "en": "so once our view has been rendered, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 252.81,
          "end": 254.64,
          "en": "And the same, AfterViewChecked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 254.64,
          "end": 257.7,
          "en": "well that is called whenever our view has been checked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 257.7,
          "end": 261.3,
          "en": "So once we are sure that, well either all changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 261.3,
          "end": 263.91,
          "en": "which had to be done were displayed in the view,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 263.91,
          "end": 266.79,
          "en": "or no changes were detected by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 266.79,
          "end": 269.46,
          "en": "And finally, if you destroy a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 269.46,
          "end": 272.1,
          "en": "for example if you placed ngIf on it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 272.1,
          "end": 274.59000000000003,
          "en": "and this gets then set to false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 274.59000000000003,
          "end": 277.23,
          "en": "and therefore it removes it from the DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 277.23,
          "end": 278.88,
          "en": "ngOnDestroy is called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 278.88,
          "end": 281.52,
          "en": "And here's a great place to do some clean up work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 281.52,
          "end": 283.38,
          "en": "because this is called right before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 283.38,
          "end": 286.71,
          "en": "the object itself will be destroyed by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 286.71,
          "end": 288.12,
          "en": "These are the hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 288.12,
          "end": 289.59000000000003,
          "en": "Nice to see them in theory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 289.59000000000003,
          "end": 291.94,
          "en": "Let's see them in practice in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
